  "scope": "Retained credential recovery owners now cover exact native scope/plan observations, partial acquisition, failed/cancelled opening, staged close retries and terminal post-descriptor-close simulation. They do not integrate a full startup factory or close-before-Complete coordinator. Isolated native credential/private-file, authenticated CREATE-plan and exact timer/worker cancellation tests, with separate real native-store/OS integration and a synthetic verifier. Seven journal tests cover real plans, encrypted control, malformed-state and legacy/provider barriers. Eleven live-setup tests retain selection-only ordering and exact retries without access. Nine setup-publication tests exercise the actual PrivateSessionRuntime composite create/retry path with real credential/data/work/control stores: an acknowledged exact journal precedes selection; a fresh changed schema2 private binding and work seal precede acknowledged Complete; only then may a lease/access view be published. Before/after seal and completion failures, missing readback, cancellation/close, exact retry, controlled reopen, mismatched operation and pending restart gates are covered. Runtime credential interruption retains all three plans and rejects credential-only abort; a separate explicit legacy test preserves native credential-only recovery proof. Control/work wrapper failures model application acknowledgement loss, not native engine sync errors; binding VFS failures are tested separately in the storage APK. Provider acquisition/restoration is synthetic, not actual provider/bootstrap/configuration approval. Selection-only data replay is not a fresh durability acknowledgement; binding completion supplies the changed private write. Native diagnostics inspect already-open stores only. Twelve credential-plan observation tests cover exact scope/native MAC, stable metadata fingerprints, key/artifact presence changes, deliberate exclusion of credential ciphertext contents, foreign/unknown/newer inventory refusal, detachment and unchanged poison/close guards. Nine interrupted composite setup tests exercise the actual already-open runtime report over all four native stores, exact plan/scope/configuration and metadata-change gates, including sole-binding validation and retained pending control. These comparisons neither read tokens nor establish credential usability or durability; they never open a recovery factory or infer confirmation. Twelve already-open credential-plan abort tests authenticate exact scope/native plan and preserve parent ownership, poison guards, unrelated files and fresh synchronization on retry. Ten real-runtime composite abort tests cover opaque evidence-bound proposals, explicit programmatic confirmation, durable true intent before ordered work/data/credential cleanup, stopped unknown acknowledgements, exact repeated retries and same-runtime retained final-control receipt recovery. No confirmation UI or provider is used, and borrowed native owners are not closed by this coordinator. Explicit readable-empty discard and legacy CREATE abort retain their separate paths. No existing-only composite startup factories or startup repair, full first-factory or generalized orphan recovery, refresh-plan, production worker/timer/domain scheduling, FeedMe UI, real sign-in, hard-kill, physical-device, power-loss, iOS or release proof. Notification and hardlink branches remain explicitly reported.",
